# Blockchain Markdown — Proof of Concept Document

<!-- bmd:rule double -->

This document is a formally structured proof-of-concept declaration, compiled and
cryptographically sealed under the **Blockchain Markdown (.bmd) Protocol v2.1**.

It demonstrates real, verifiable Ed25519 signatures and SHA-512 ledger hashing.
This file is the canonical, tamper-evident record — the standalone HTML viewer
derived from it is purely a rendering layer; the cryptographic truth lives here.

<!-- bmd:parties -->

<!-- bmd:rule single -->

<!-- bmd:clause 1 Purpose and Scope -->

This block serves as a live demonstration of the Blockchain Markdown immutability
protocol. Once compiled, no character of the payload may be altered without
invalidating the SHA-512 ledger hash and Ed25519 digital signature.

<!-- bmd:clause 2 Cryptographic Standards Applied -->

| Standard | Algorithm | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Payload Integrity** | SHA-512 (128 hex chars) | Tamper-evident content lock |
| **Identity & Signing** | Ed25519 Elliptic Curve | Non-repudiation of authorship |
| **Key Generation** | RFC 8032 seed derivation | Deterministic keypair from 32-byte seed |
| **Co-Signature** | Ed25519 (second party) | Bilateral consensus ratification |

<!-- bmd:clause 3 Immutability Guarantee -->

Upon compilation to `mode: transfer`, the following actions become permanently
forbidden by the engine:

- Editing any byte of the payload
- Altering any frontmatter field
- Adding, removing, or modifying signatures beyond the `max_signatures` cap
- Forking this block (a new block with a new `block_id` must be created instead)

The document is rendered in a standalone zero-dependency HTML file that can be
verified in any modern browser without installing any software, library, or runtime.

<!-- bmd:rule double -->

